551
00:38:55,084 --> 00:38:58,125
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as I said, you don't actually blame the food, but you have to eat.

552
00:38:58,565 --> 00:39:00,586
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then you do, okay, so I just have to eat this food.

553
00:39:01,126 --> 00:39:03,227
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then I'll just take great care.

554
00:39:04,315 --> 00:39:08,276
[SPEAKER_01]: To avoid swallowing and biting and chewing into the bait.

555
00:39:08,756 --> 00:39:09,236
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's it.

556
00:39:10,117 --> 00:39:11,257
[SPEAKER_01]: Bait is a foreign object.

557
00:39:13,117 --> 00:39:15,678
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's the body's business, food.

558
00:39:15,878 --> 00:39:16,698
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

559
00:39:16,838 --> 00:39:18,039
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not your business, really.

560
00:39:19,079 --> 00:39:23,220
[SPEAKER_00]: Which you have to attend to every day.

561
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:28,621
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it means every day you need to be mindful of the bait.

562
00:39:29,001 --> 00:39:31,442
[SPEAKER_01]: Every day you need to be mindful of the trap and the snare.

563
00:39:33,292 --> 00:39:41,198
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the practice is basically about everyday mindfulness and that repetitive drilling.

564
00:39:41,738 --> 00:39:58,251
[SPEAKER_00]: Drilling is quite a burden, isn't it?

565
00:40:02,730 --> 00:40:03,070
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, no.

566
00:40:03,150 --> 00:40:09,094
[SPEAKER_01]: Mara is a bird, because he's relentless in having that bait placed in the food.

567
00:40:11,996 --> 00:40:17,399
[SPEAKER_01]: So... but again, he has every right to do so, because the food belongs to him.

568
00:40:18,940 --> 00:40:22,282
[SPEAKER_01]: The food, the taste, and the tongue belongs to him.

569
00:40:22,802 --> 00:40:25,363
[SPEAKER_01]: The sights and eyes belong to him.

570
00:40:25,804 --> 00:40:27,705
[SPEAKER_01]: The sounds and ears belong to him.

571
00:40:28,485 --> 00:40:29,526
[SPEAKER_01]: Remember, that's what the Buddha said.

572
00:40:30,027 --> 00:40:32,787
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because people take that which belongs to Mara.

573
00:40:33,228 --> 00:40:36,368
[SPEAKER_01]: Mara does what he wants with them, on account of it.

574
00:40:37,148 --> 00:40:38,308
[SPEAKER_01]: And what is that he takes?

575
00:40:38,488 --> 00:40:39,929
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the eye and the sights.

576
00:40:40,029 --> 00:40:41,489
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the ear and the sounds.

577
00:40:41,549 --> 00:40:42,929
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the nose and the smells.

578
00:40:43,309 --> 00:40:46,070
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you realize, he, the senses, your senses actually belong to him.

579
00:40:46,390 --> 00:40:48,570
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he has every right to put whatever he wants in it.

580
00:40:50,791 --> 00:40:56,712
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's you who keeps biting careless and then hooking yourself like a mindless fish.

581
00:40:58,392 --> 00:40:59,412
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's just, eh...

582
00:41:01,575 --> 00:41:04,137
[SPEAKER_01]: That's just basically... that's the deal.

583
00:41:04,297 --> 00:41:05,298
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what saṃsāra is.

584
00:41:05,318 --> 00:41:06,538
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what existence is.

585
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:13,924
[SPEAKER_01]: A person can complain about it, feel sorry for himself, but that's just how it is.

586
00:41:15,945 --> 00:41:23,390
[SPEAKER_01]: And you will complain about it, feel sorry, because you're still refusing to give up your ownership of those things.

587
00:41:23,410 --> 00:41:27,092
[SPEAKER_01]: You still feel entitled to that, to your eyes and to the sights.

588
00:41:28,033 --> 00:41:29,134
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, because I was here first.

589
00:41:29,594 --> 00:41:30,555
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, exactly.

